---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import portrait from '../assets/jt-portrait.png';
import '../styles/home.css';
---

<Base home>
<div class="shell">
  <header class="id">
    <figure class="portrait" id="portrait" tabindex="0" role="img" aria-label="JT Porter leaning against a cinderblock wall, smiling, in a white tee and jeans. Drag to move; it snaps to the grid. Arrow keys move it, Escape puts it back."><Image src={portrait} alt="" widths={[240, 480]} sizes="10rem" loading="eager" draggable="false" /></figure>
    <p class="drag-hint" id="drag-hint" data-i18n="hint_photo">Drag me. I snap to the grid.</p>
    <h1>JT Porter</h1>
    <p class="role" data-i18n="role">Senior Software Engineer</p>
    <p class="open"><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span data-i18n="open">Open to work · Remote preferred</span></p>
    <p class="pitch" data-i18n="pitch">I build interfaces people can grab, drag, and rely on, for resorts, families, and patients.</p>
    <ul class="nav">
      <li><a href="#about" data-i18n="nav_about">About</a></li>
      <li><a href="#now" data-i18n="nav_now">TimeShareWare</a></li>
      <li><a href="#experience" data-i18n="nav_exp">Experience</a></li>
      <li><a href="#work" data-i18n="nav_work">Projects</a></li>
      <li><a href="#contact" data-i18n="nav_contact">Contact</a></li>
    </ul>
    <div class="foot">
      <a href="mailto:jtporter9@gmail.com">Email</a>
      <a href="https://github.com/jtporter9">GitHub</a>
      <a href="https://linkedin.com/in/jtporter9">LinkedIn</a>
      <a href="/resume" data-i18n="resume">Resume</a>
      <span class="lang" role="group" aria-label="Language">
        <button type="button" id="lang-en" aria-pressed="true">EN</button>
        <button type="button" id="lang-es" aria-pressed="false">ES</button>
      </span>
    </div>
  </header>

  <main class="story" id="main">
    <section id="about" class="about">
      <h2 class="label" data-i18n="nav_about">About</h2>
        <p data-i18n="about1">For the last four years I was a senior engineer at <strong>TimeShareWare</strong>, where I rebuilt the <strong>Room Matrix</strong>, the drag-and-drop board resort companies like Vidanta and Hyatt use to manage thousands of rooms, and cut its load time from as long as 90 seconds to 10 or less. It’s the kind of UI I love: dense, fast, and hard to get right.</p>
        <p data-i18n="about2">Before that I led a team of seven at <strong>Readeo</strong> to ship a family reading app, and I was one of the first five employees at <strong>LowestMed</strong>, which grew 7x and was acquired by RetailMeNot.</p>
        <p data-i18n="about3">I work mostly in React and TypeScript, lean on Claude Code every day, and am happy to pair on a problem in English or Spanish. I’m looking for a long-term team where I can stay hands-on and help shape the architecture and design decisions that make a product better.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="now" class="feature">
      <h2 class="label" data-i18n="nav_now">TimeShareWare</h2>
      <p class="feature-meta" data-i18n="tsw_meta">Most recent · Senior Software Engineer · 2022 — 2026</p>
      <h2 class="big" data-i18n="tsw_title">Building the tools resorts run on</h2>
      <p class="lede" data-i18n="tsw_lede">TimeShareWare makes the platform that 7–10 resort companies, including Vidanta and Hyatt, use to run hundreds of resorts. On a UI team of about seven, I built in React, Redux, and TypeScript on a C# / .NET backend, reviewed code, ran releases, and was the go-to engineer for design and styling.</p>

      <dl class="stats">
        <div><dt data-i18n="st1">Room Matrix load time</dt><dd>30–90s → 1–10s</dd></div>
        <div><dt data-i18n="st2">Rebuild</dt><dd data-i18n="st2v">~2 months</dd></div>
        <div><dt data-i18n="st3">Scale</dt><dd data-i18n="st3v">100s of resorts</dd></div>
      </dl>

      <div class="demo-head">
        <h3 class="sub" data-i18n="demo_title">The Room Matrix</h3>
        <span class="chip" data-i18n="sample">Sample data</span>
      </div>
      <p class="demo-intro" data-i18n="demo_intro">A tiny version of the board I rebuilt. Drag a stay or a maintenance block to another room or night. Overlaps are rejected, just like the real thing.</p>
      <div class="board-wrap">
        <div class="board" id="board">
          <div></div>
          <div class="days" id="days"></div>
          <div class="rooms" id="rooms"></div>
          <div class="lanes" id="lanes"></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="status" id="status" aria-live="polite"></p>

      <ul class="built">
        <li><span data-i18n="b1"><strong>Rebuilt the Room Matrix with drag-and-drop.</strong> Staff assign reservations to rooms, move dates, and block rooms for maintenance right on the board.</span></li>
        <li><span data-i18n="b2"><strong>Replaced a board that couldn’t drag at all</strong> and had recurring problems assigning rooms and displaying stays correctly.</span></li>
        <li><span data-i18n="b3"><strong>Made it fast.</strong> A faster data API and lazy loading took load times from 30–90 seconds down to 1–10, across thousands of rooms.</span></li>
      </ul>

      <div class="pillars">
        <div><h4 data-i18n="pl1">Reservation booking</h4><p data-i18n="pl1d">Built the room search, booking, and usage/points payment screens, wired closely to backend APIs.</p></div>
        <div><h4 data-i18n="pl2">Design &amp; styling lead</h4><p data-i18n="pl2d">Implemented the modernized look and feel across much of the app.</p></div>
        <div><h4 data-i18n="pl3">AI-assisted dev</h4><p data-i18n="pl3d">Early Claude Code adopter. Taught the team Claude Skills and set up our shared AI context.</p></div>
      </div>
      <a class="cv" href="/work/room-matrix" data-i18n="rm_more">Read the Room Matrix story →</a>
    </section>

    <section id="experience">
      <h2 class="label" data-i18n="nav_exp">Experience</h2>
      <ol class="jobs">
        <li class="job current">
          <div class="when">2022 — 2026</div>
          <div>
            <h3>Senior Software Engineer <span>· TimeShareWare</span></h3>
            <p data-i18n="j_tsw">Rebuilt the Room Matrix (30–90s → 1–10s loads), built core booking screens, and led UI modernization for resort companies like Vidanta and Hyatt.</p>
            <ul class="tags"><li>React</li><li>TypeScript</li><li>Redux</li><li>C# / .NET</li><li>Claude Code</li></ul>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="job">
          <div class="when">2020 — 2022</div>
          <div>
            <h3>Engineering Team Lead <span>· Readeo</span></h3>
            <p data-i18n="j_readeo">Hired as lead. Ran a team of 7 engineers plus sprints and planning, and launched the Readeo app on the App Store and Google Play.</p>
            <ul class="tags"><li>React</li><li>Redux</li><li>Node.js</li><li>Leadership</li></ul>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="job">
          <div class="when">2019 — 2020</div>
          <div>
            <h3>Software Engineer <span>· Principal Financial Group</span></h3>
            <p data-i18n="j_pfg">Helped build the design library used across the whole Fortune 250 company, and shipped updates to principal.com.</p>
            <ul class="tags"><li>Design systems</li><li>Drupal</li></ul>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="job">
          <div class="when">2018 — 2019</div>
          <div>
            <h3>Software Engineer <span>· RetailMeNot</span></h3>
            <p data-i18n="j_rmn">Migrated Rx Saver from Angular to React/Redux and raised test coverage 40%. Rx Saver was later acquired by GoodRx.</p>
            <ul class="tags"><li>React</li><li>Redux</li><li>Jest</li></ul>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="job">
          <div class="when">2016 — 2018</div>
          <div>
            <h3>Full-Stack Engineer <span>· LowestMed</span></h3>
            <p data-i18n="j_lm">Employee #5. Helped move the product from Angular to React, built search-as-you-type drug lookup, and helped build a system that faxed files to pharmacies and doctors, as monthly transactions grew from 7k to 50k+.</p>
            <ul class="tags"><li>Angular → React</li><li>.NET</li><li>SQL</li></ul>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ol>
      <a class="cv" href="/resume" data-i18n="cv">View full résumé →</a>
    </section>

    <section id="work">
      <h2 class="label" data-i18n="nav_work">Projects</h2>
      <ul class="projects">
        <li><a href="/work/room-matrix"><span class="stat">1–10s</span><h3 data-i18n="p_rm">Rebuilding the Room Matrix</h3><p data-i18n="p_rm_d">Load time after the rebuild, down from 30–90 seconds, for hundreds of resorts.</p><span class="more" data-i18n="more">Read the story →</span></a></li>
        <li><a href="/work/lowestmed"><span class="stat">7k→50k+</span><h3 data-i18n="p_lm">Employee #5 to acquisition</h3><p data-i18n="p_lm_d">Monthly transactions at LowestMed before RetailMeNot bought it.</p><span class="more" data-i18n="more">Read the story →</span></a></li>
        <li><a href="/work/rx-saver"><span class="stat">+40%</span><h3 data-i18n="p_rx">Rewriting Rx Saver in React</h3><p data-i18n="p_rx_d">Frontend test coverage after the Angular → React migration.</p><span class="more" data-i18n="more">Read the story →</span></a></li>
        <li><a href="/work/readeo"><span class="stat">7</span><h3 data-i18n="p_rd">Leading a team to the app stores</h3><p data-i18n="p_rd_d">Engineers I led to launch Readeo on iOS and Android.</p><span class="more" data-i18n="more">Read the story →</span></a></li>
        <li><a href="https://havenwellness.com"><span class="stat" data-i18n="p_hw_s">Live</span><h3>Haven Wellness</h3><p data-i18n="p_hw_d">Side project: helped build the website for a wellness business.</p><span class="more" data-i18n="visit">Visit the site →</span></a></li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="contact" class="contact">
      <h2 class="label" data-i18n="nav_contact">Contact</h2>
      <p class="feature-meta"><span data-i18n="open">Open to work · Remote preferred</span></p>
      <h2 class="big" data-i18n="ct_title">Let’s build something together</h2>
      <p class="lede" data-i18n="ct_body">I’m looking for senior frontend, full-stack, AI software engineering, or engineering lead roles, ideally remote, with a team I can grow with for the long haul. The fastest way to reach me is email or LinkedIn.</p>
      <p class="ct-links">
        <a class="btn" href="mailto:jtporter9@gmail.com">jtporter9@gmail.com</a>
        <a class="btn ghost" href="https://linkedin.com/in/jtporter9">LinkedIn</a>
        <a class="btn ghost" href="/resume" data-i18n="resume">Resume</a>
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
</div>
</Base>

<script>
  import '../scripts/home.js';
</script>
